 r←RenderConfigJson json;patterns
⍝ Returns the lines of a package config file ready to be shown on its "details" page: escaped,
⍝ with keys, strings and numbers in spans that give them their colours, URLs as links and the
⍝ group leading to its home page, if it has one.
⍝ It works line by line and pattern by pattern rather than parsing the JSON, so the page shows
⍝ the file exactly as it was published, order and spacing included.
⍝ The order of the patterns matters twice over. ⎕R tries them in this order at every position,
⍝ so a URL is recognised before it can pass for an ordinary string, and the digits inside a
⍝ string are never taken for a number. And `RenderJsonToken` tells them apart by position.
 patterns←⊂'^(\s*)([A-Za-z_]\w*)(\s*:)'             ⍝ 0: a key, with the blanks before it and its colon
 patterns,←⊂'"https?://[^"]*"'                      ⍝ 1: a string that is a URL
 patterns,←⊂'"[^"]*"'                               ⍝ 2: any other string
 patterns,←⊂'-?\b\d+(?:\.\d+)?\b'                   ⍝ 3: a number
 r←patterns ⎕R RenderJsonToken⊢EscapeSpecialChars json
⍝Done
